# ATMOS — COMPLETE FUNCTIONALITY, CUSTOMIZATION & QUALITY OVERHAUL

## Role and mission

You are the senior Android engineer, UI/UX engineer, weather-data engineer and QA engineer responsible for finishing **Atmos**, an existing native Android weather application.

The existing generated UI is PERFECT. The visual direction has already been approved.

**Your job is NOT to redesign Atmos from scratch. Your job is to preserve its existing visual identity, inspect the entire project, and transform it into a genuinely functional, highly customizable Android weather application.**

The current project has major shortcomings:
- Some controls are decorative or do nothing.
- Customization options are insufficient.
- Android permissions and background functionality are incomplete.
- Weather providers are not properly configurable.
- Radar and maps need real data and interaction.
- Weather alerts need to work.
- Gyroscope parallax needs to be significantly stronger.
- Weather illustrations look cheap and need professional-quality assets.
- The application must be tested beyond simply rendering its screens.

Do not just explain how to fix these issues. Inspect the existing project and implement the fixes in the actual codebase.

If a tool, API, credential or external service is unavailable, identify the blocker and implement the best working alternative without fabricating successful functionality.

