# 9. MUCH STRONGER GYROSCOPE PARALLAX

The current parallax effect is too weak.

Make it noticeably more expressive while keeping it smooth and comfortable.

## 9.1 Motion model

Use the Android rotation vector sensor where available.

Use a stable sensor-processing approach that avoids jitter and abrupt jumps.

Implement layered parallax:
- Foreground weather objects move the most.
- Midground clouds and objects move moderately.
- Background sky and distant scenery move subtly.
- Additional atmospheric elements can move at different rates.

Use smooth interpolation and clamp movement to safe limits.

Do not tilt the text or temperature so much that readability suffers.

## 9.2 Customization

Provide a real parallax control in Settings:
- Off.
- Subtle.
- Balanced.
- Strong.
- Custom intensity slider, if practical.

The Strong option must be clearly more visible than the current implementation.

Apply intensity consistently to supported illustrations.

Allow the user to preview the effect in Settings.

## 9.3 Lifecycle and accessibility

- Subscribe to sensors only when appropriate.
- Stop sensor processing when the relevant screen is not visible.
- Handle devices without suitable sensors.
- Prevent sudden jumps after resuming the app.
- Avoid unnecessary battery consumption.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences.
- Keep a static fallback available.

Do not simulate sensor movement using random animations.

## 9.4 Animation controls

Also provide:
- Global animation toggle.
- Weather animation toggle.
- Parallax toggle.
- Animation intensity.
- Reduced-motion mode.
- Optional static artwork mode.

Every control must change actual behaviour.

